Problem Statement:
Given an array, move every element one position to the left, and move the first element to the last position.


Approach:
Store the first element in a temporary variable because it will be overwritten.
Shift every remaining element one position towards the left.
Place the stored first element at the last index.


Code:
class Solution {
public:
    void rotateArrayByOne(vector<int>& nums) {

        int n = nums.size();

        // If the array has 0 or 1 element, no rotation is needed.
        if (n <= 1)
            return;

        int temp = nums[0];

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            nums[i - 1] = nums[i];
        }

        nums[n - 1] = temp;
    }
};


Time Complexity : O(n)
Space Complexity : O(n)
